GAP-002 minimum-host-floor qualification — Unity 6000.0.84f1 on the licensed macOS host (2026-09-27)

Purpose: re-verify the GAP-002 recorded blocker after a harness change (the fleet now offers a
licensed Unity host). The package's declared minimum host version is Unity 6000.0 (`unity: "6000.0"`
in unity/com.noisemaker.hlsl/package.json); this run exercises that floor first-hand on a licensed
editor, which the 2026-09-26 passes 17/18 could not (their Linux editors exited 198 with 0 entitlements).

Host: macOS 26.6.2 (Build 25G83), Darwin 25.6.0, ARM64 (Apple Silicon), 32 GB.
License: machine-wide `/Library/Application Support/Unity/Unity_lic.ulf` (pre-existing on the host;
  automation performed no activation). The 6000.3.16f1 editor on the same host uses the same license.
Editor: Unity 6000.0.84f1, changeset 78ab6fc243d5 (the same release the pass-18 Linux floor run used).
  Source: official https://download.unity3d.com/download_unity/78ab6fc243d5/MacEditorInstaller/Unity.pkg
  sha256 3df66b594b3acbe5938cec52d12f8eeaf41df6e8049c3ff1e9b395dda244870b (4,989,558,815 bytes).
  Installed unattended WITHOUT admin rights: `pkgutil --expand-full Unity.pkg expanded` (no `installer`,
  no root); the app runs from the extracted path. The editor binary is x86_64 and runs under Rosetta on
  this ARM64 host (editor's own log header: "Architecture: x86_64 / Running under Rosetta: YES").
Package under test: unity/com.noisemaker.hlsl embedded from this repository at source
  12a4be35957e7d0b4533841b7894c8587f8d3e82 (current main, clean, matches origin/main).

Legs (exact commands, verbatim exit codes):

1) Fresh project: $UNITY -batchmode -quit -createProject /tmp/u6000/proj -logFile create.log  -> exit 0
2) Color space per Quick Start README: ProjectSettings.asset m_ActiveColorSpace: 0 -> 1 (Linear);
   grep confirms: m_ActiveColorSpace: 1
3) Embedded package + Quick Start sample copied (Packages/com.noisemaker.hlsl, Assets/QuickStart).
   Import: $UNITY -batchmode -quit -projectPath /tmp/u6000/proj -logFile import.log -> exit 0;
   `grep -c "error CS"` -> 0 (no compile errors).
4) Runtime harness: $UNITY -batchmode -quit -projectPath /tmp/u6000/proj -executeMethod
   Noisemaker.Hlsl.Editor.NMOutputRuntimeTests.VerifyFromCommandLine -logFile tests.log -> exit 0;
   log ends "Exiting batchmode successfully now!". Full log appended below.
5) Quick Start render leg: $UNITY -batchmode -quit -projectPath /tmp/u6000/proj -executeMethod
   Noisemaker.Hlsl.Editor.NMParityRunner.RenderFromCommandLine -nmGraph
   /tmp/u6000/proj/Assets/QuickStart/NoiseGraph.json -nmOut /tmp/u6000/qs6000.png -nmSize 512
   -nmTime 0.25 -logFile render.log
   The render SUCCEEDED: log records "[NMParity] registered 212/212 package shaders by name." and
   "[NMParity] wrote /tmp/u6000/qs6000.png (512x512, time=0.25)". The editor process then crashed
   during -quit shutdown (shell exit code 139, SIGSEGV) — reproduced identically on a second run
   (render2.log): same write line, byte-identical output
   qs6000.png / qs6000-r2.png sha256 0da6bc7599f89859f75515f4edbb6d48bbf6f688619962b9c57c86f49bc294b7
   (444,389 bytes each). The crash is after EditorApplication.Exit(0) is invoked and after the output
   was written and flushed; it is recorded truthfully as a 6000.0.84f1 shutdown artifact of this
   extracted-editor configuration, not a package failure (to be re-checked if this editor or
   configuration is exercised on other hosts). Rendered PNG measured locally:
   512x512 RGBA, mean 111.47, 234 distinct gray levels, 100% non-black pixels — meaningful output.

Verbatim host transcripts follow (create/import excerpted, tests + both render logs in full).
